url: "https://github.com/u39kun/ads-two-shell-chaos"
abstract: >-
  Simulation, analysis, and figure code, with the saved results, for a study of
  two concentric thin shells that interact through gravity and pass through each
  other in anti-de Sitter space. It computes the return map of the shells to a
  section of their crossings, its invariant measure, a variational tangent and
  finite-time exponents, scans of chaotic orbits near the saddle and across the
  type (ii) family of initial data of Brito, Cardoso, and Rocha, and a validation
  against their results.
keywords:
  - anti-de Sitter
  - thin shells
  - general relativity
  - Poincaré section
  - area-preserving map
  - finite-time Lyapunov exponents
  - chaos
